CSO Housing App — Meeting Notes
Date: November 16
1. Long-Term Direction
- Long-term goal: expand the service to all undergraduate housing.
- Current scope: graduate housing only.
- Future scope: campus-wide service.
- The system should be compatible with computers and cell phones.
- The long-term goal is to transition to an app-only experience.
2. Information and Tracking Requirements
The system should track and retain:
- Name.
- Housing location.
- PID.
- Request status.
- Service and response information.
- Number of requests and lockouts.
- Request time and duration.
- Housing location statistics.
Housing should have access to both:
- The existing Google Form information.
- Information submitted through the application.
The user should sign off and verify that they will pay the $25 service fee.

The application should eventually be presented to Housing for review and adoption.
3. SSO Option
- Revisit the single sign-on (SSO) option after meeting with Housing.
4. CSO Workflow and Devices
Current Device
- CSOs currently use a company phone.
Future Device
- The long-term plan may use a tablet.
Required CSO Features
- Receive service requests.
- View pending requests.
- Receive pop-up notifications when a request is submitted.
- Respond to requests.
- Notify users of their estimated time of arrival or position in line.
- Provide the estimated number of requests ahead in the queue.
5. Current Tracking System
- The current tracking system uses a Google Sheet.
- HDH has access to the Google Sheet to view request counts and exact request information.
- During holiday hours, many calls may arrive at the same time, making it difficult or impossible for CSOs to answer every call.
6. Sgt. King’s Recommendations
- Continue using a mobile website embedded with the Google Form as an initial approach.
- Track statistics such as:
  - Time.
  - Number of requests.
  - Housing location.
  - Quantity of lockouts.
- Example metric: approximately 40 lockouts in Nuevo East during a holiday period.
- After confirmation, complete the sign-off and service process through the application.
- Provide users with the ability to cancel a service request.
- Account for high staff turnover and frequent personnel changes.
- Allow CSOs to sign in using their name and badge number.
7. Front-End Form Categories
The front end should include a user category selector, such as:
- Sublessee.
- Family member.
- Student.
Potential email validation rules:
- Family members or sublessees may use Gmail or another email domain.
- Students may use a UCSD email address ending in ucsd.edu.
